WHAT IS BROKEN — measured on f284b3b (current ai/main), not replayed:

  `python3 scripts/slot_reader_probe.py` on this tree answers rc 1,
  "readers matching: 2 of 3", RED naming `guard-curslot`: the exact grep shipped
  at agent-team.yml:1091 cannot find the exact slot line shipped in
  agent-team/TEAM-CONTROL.org. Reproduced directly against the register file:

    grep -Ec '^\#+PENDING-REVIEW:' agent-team/TEAM-CONTROL.org   -> 0
    grep -Ec '^#\+PENDING-REVIEW:' agent-team/TEAM-CONTROL.org   -> 1

  GNU grep 3.11 (this image, `grep --version`) reads the ERE escape `\#+` as an
  ordinary `#` followed by the one-or-more quantifier — "one-or-more hash
  characters" — which the register line `#+PENDING-REVIEW: ...` does NOT contain
  (it carries exactly one hash before the P). Undefined-escape dialect, resolved
  silently, in the direction that hides the line.

  Why that specific line matters — the guard depends on it being TRUE: the
  non-clobber condition at :1094 is
  `if [ -n "$NEWPENDING" ] || [ -z "$CURSLOT" ] || { ... }`, and with an
  always-empty CURSLOT the middle disjunct is ALWAYS true, so every empty write
  is admitted — the exact 27748d9 clobber shape (Lead 10-am: "wrote 'next
  pending: none' and wiped the register EMPTY") that ed378d4 built this guard to
  refuse. The guard is armed but blind: the law landed, its read does not work,
  and chain_slot_check.py's `blank-guard` leg — a TEXT read — passes the whole
  time because the guard does mention the key and does carry the control-file
  operand. That gap (text-read legs passing while the command they describe is
  inert) is precisely why ai/turn-20261024-1552 shipped slot_reader_probe.py;
  it landed with 2326@b1d3280 and this is its first firing on the live tree.

  Consequence for right now: none yet — 10-dl advanced the register by hand to
  0015@2754f09 — but the next finalize that resolves a branch without a new
  pending (NEWPENDING empty) is licensed by this bug to blank the register, and
  the queue holds ten more branches.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES:

  Uses the merger-reread's OWN proven dialect — :871 reads the same key with
  `^#\+` (backslash-escaped plus = the quantifier on a literal `+`, which is
  exactly what the Org keyword is) and the probe shows that command FINDS the
  live line. Same key, same file, one dialect for all three slot readers. The
  sed write address at :1095 is deliberately NOT touched: GNU sed reads `\#+` as
  hash-then-one-or-more-`+` and the probe's third reader proves it MOVES the
  line — this patch fixes the measured defect, one character, and re-cuts
  nothing that is green.

ON LANDING (Lead): relabel this file `STATUS: RETIRED` and DELETE the APPLY line,
  naming `GRADED BY: scripts/slot_reader_probe.py` — that probe flips to rc 0
  ("3/3") the moment the hunk is in, and chain_patch_check's GRADE leg then keeps
  the retirement measured by the command itself, never by this text. If instead
  the Lead lands the fix REWORDED (any dialect that makes guard-curslot FIND the
  line), that satisfies the law — do not re-apply this hunk then; relabel per
